{"schema_version": 1, "id": "37fd99f6-dc47-4d10-834b-cc8f96804f6e", "stream": {"kind": "session", "id": "01a08e34-e8e6-7042-a91b-e25ac02b6cff"}, "sequence": 51, "recorded_at": 1789092239800829, "record_type": "event", "durability": "durable", "causation_id": null, "payload_type": "runtime.session", "payload_schema_version": 1, "payload": {"event": {"kind": "assistant_message_committed", "message_id": "181365b9-907c-4d4d-90ba-bdc60505ba3f", "provider_item_id": "msg_01a08e351549720288018a675af13cf2", "response_id": "resp_6aa3618490691b012a294777", "text": "The moduli are pairwise coprime, so there is a unique solution mod $7\\cdot 11\\cdot 13\\cdot 17\\cdot 19 = 323323$.\n\nSolving successively:\n\n* $n\\equiv 3\\pmod 7$, $n\\equiv 5\\pmod{11}$ gives $n\\equiv 38\\pmod{77}$\n* with $n\\equiv 8\\pmod{13}$ gives $n\\equiv 346\\pmod{1001}$\n* with $n\\equiv 11\\pmod{17}$ gives $n\\equiv 6352\\pmod{17017}$\n* with $n\\equiv 13\\pmod{19}$ gives $n\\equiv 312658\\pmod{323323}$\n\nSo the smallest positive integer is\n\n$$n = 312658$$\n\nVerification:\n\n* $312658 = 7\\cdot 44665 + 3$\n* $312658 = 11\\cdot 28423 + 5$\n* $312658 = 13\\cdot 24050 + 8$\n* $312658 = 17\\cdot 18391 + 11$\n* $312658 = 19\\cdot 16455 + 13$\n\nDONE\n"}, "kind": "run", "run_id": "c2891d4f-85b6-44fe-946c-a6f0ea031e2b", "source_run_record_id": "a5dcdd56-2827-4ba0-b68b-fe7d2a583f14", "source_run_record_sequence": 43}}
